  o Minor features (denial-of-service, onion service directory):
    - Add the HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop option and consensus parameter, off by
      default. It lets an HSDir refuse onion service descriptor requests whose
      previous hop is not a known relay, by closing their circuit. Refused
      requests are counted as action "refused" in tor_relay_hsdir_fetch_total
      and tor_relay_hsdir_upload_total. Part of ticket 41339.
    - Add the HSDirDescriptorFetchRate and HSDirDescriptorFetchBurst options.
      An HSDir counts fetches of each cached onion service descriptor over that
      rate as tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_fetch_over_rate"} on the
      MetricsPort, which shows whether a flood of fetches concentrates on a few
      descriptors. Part of ticket 41339.
    - Add the HSDirFetchShedding and HSDirFetchBudget options, and the
      HSDirFetchShedding and HSDirFetchBudgetPercent consensus parameters. When
      enabled (off by default), an HSDir that is asked for more onion service
      descriptor bytes in a second than its budget sheds fetches in that second
      and the next, answering first those within their descriptor's
      HSDirDescriptorFetchRate. Until then, it refuses nothing. Such fetches
      are counted on the MetricsPort whether or not it is enabled. Part of
      ticket 41339.
